WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.547
This query calculates each sale's percent of all revenue.

00:00:03.547 --> 00:00:08.902
SUM revenue OVER empty parentheses means the window covers all returned rows.

00:00:08.902 --> 00:00:12.737
There is no partition. Each sale remains in the output.

00:00:12.737 --> 00:00:16.332
Run the query and inspect the largest contributions.

00:00:16.332 --> 00:00:21.157
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:21.157 --> 00:00:25.317
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:25.317 --> 00:00:29.607
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:29.607 --> 00:00:35.432
In a real setting such as a sales team calculating running revenue and top products by region,

00:00:35.432 --> 00:00:41.672
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:41.672 --> 00:00:43.232
before discussing syntax.

00:00:43.232 --> 00:00:49.128
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
